# Lines tools/qemu-test must see, in this order, as whole serial lines - all
# printed by the console PD through the UART's own registers, so the same in
# the debug and the release configuration (supervisor-panic.configs).
# A child panics; the supervisor reads the fault's label before
# parsing it, reports it undecoded, survives, and resets the board; the
# system boots again. The "fault detail" line names the label, which differs
# between the two kernels, and is not checked.
NOWAYOS: console: starting
NOWAYOS: supervisor: starting; children console (0) and panicker (1)
NOWAYOS: supervisor: panicker stopped: a fault the supervisor does not decode
NOWAYOS: supervisor: resetting the board
NOWAYOS: console: starting
NOWAYOS: supervisor: starting; children console (0) and panicker (1)
NOWAYOS: supervisor: panicker stopped: a fault the supervisor does not decode

# Output that fails the test at once if it appears anywhere (substring match):
# the reset returning, a fault the monitor had to handle (the supervisor or
# the console faulted), a kernel error message, or a line the console refused.
!the reset returned
!NOT stopped
!MON|ERROR
!seL4(CPU
!refused
!no children are defined
!gave up
